#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rain Drops"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Raindrops</emphasis> filter puts beautiful raindrops "
"on your image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Raindrops</emphasis> is nice little tool to put raindrops onto "
"your images. Naturally, it renders your image in a kind of wet look. It uses "
"an algorithm copyrighted by Pieter Voloshyn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Raindrops filter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Raindrops Tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Three sliders give you control over the effect filter:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Drop size</guilabel> obviously allows to change the size of the "
"drops. As the drop size doesn't automatically scale with the image size it "
"is often necessary to reduce the size for small images. <guilabel>Number</"
"guilabel> changes the number and density of drops. <guilabel>Fish eye</"
"guilabel> changes the optical effect of the drops across the image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can keep a zone clear of raindrops with the &digikam; Image Editor "
"<guilabel>Select</guilabel> tool. Selecting the area to avoid (for example a "
"face) before launching the <emphasis>Raindrops</emphasis> filter will keep "
"it free from rain drops."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Raindrops filter in action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is an example of the raindrops filter. The original image (1) shows a "
"quiet sunset, the transformed image (2) indicates a sunset after a "
"thunderstorm. Default values have been used for this example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-filters-raindrops.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rain Drops Image Effect Preview"
msgstr ""

